    <processInformation>
        <dataSetInformation>
            <common:UUID>bc7dfcbd-1656-3133-a481-81fd9f749183</common:UUID>
            <name>
                <baseName xml:lang="en">Integrated circuit, IC, memory type, at plant</baseName>
            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="57aded3d-4d3f-3d65-b03a-7392ab36aef2">electronics</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="6086e8b4-40cc-356e-837f-debbd03b1a27">component</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">This dataset can be applied to describe the entire production of a memory type integrated circuit. The included wafer fabrication data refers to a 200-mm wafer for a 32 MB DRAM chip, whereas the chip packaging data describes the material contents (in percent) of a plastic leaded chip carrier (PLCC) microchip (years 2002 to 2004). In 2023, the dataset is updated using the technical parameters found in the report of Umweltbundesamt (UBA) 2021. This update mainly relates the energy and heat consumption, as well as the gold input for ICs. Specifically for the gold input, the mass of gold per kg IC is taken from the average values in the study of Kuo et al 2020. The regionalization to the datasets is applied for the Eastern Asia electricity mix and global average, primary metal flows. The amount of wafer required (m2) to produce 1 kg IC is taken from the empirical study of Teehan 2013; UUID: bc7dfcbd-1656-3133-a481-81fd9f749183</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
        <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
            <referenceToReferenceFlow>1</referenceToReferenceFlow>
        </quantitativeReference>
        <time xmlns:olca="http://openlca.org/ilcd-extensions" olca:startDate="1672527600000" olca:endDate="1890774000000">
            <common:referenceYear>2023</common:referenceYear>
            <common:dataSetValidUntil>2029</common:dataSetValidUntil>
            <common:timeRepresentativenessDescription xml:lang="en">Unspecified</common:timeRepresentativenessDescription>
        </time>
        <geography>
            <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="GLO">
                <descriptionOfRestrictions xml:lang="en">The data is based on a semiconductor company in the USA representing international standard.</descriptionOfRestrictions>
            </locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction>
        </geography>
        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">This dataset describes the chip packaging technology with the typical operation classes die separation, encapsulation, die attachment, lead bonding, plating and marking (inventoried only in form of consumed energy) for a memory-type microchip.\n\n# Included processes\nDescribes all the processes required to produce a memory type microchip. Included are 'die separation', 'encapsulation', 'die attachment', 'lead bonding', 'plating', and 'marking'. These operations are represented by the material input of copper alloy, epoxy resin, doped silicon, glue, gold (wires) etc. and the assembly process energy used. The required the infrastructure, and the ship, train and road transport are also inventoried. Calculated for 1 kg of packaged memory IC.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
